  "body": "[Here](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/INSTALL.md#registering-a-user) it says I should run `source ~/synapse/env/bin/activate` but the truth is that I should not do that if I've installed synapse through Ubuntu `apt-get install`. Neither should I run `synctl start`.\r\n\r\nSomeone told me that in the chatroom. But I wasted a lot of time trying to make it work.\r\n\r\nI think these instructions should clarify this.\r\n\r\nAlso this line should point to the right config file, which is not (as the line suggest) `homeserver.yml` at `$HOME`, so I guess that line also needs to be fixed.\r\n\r\nThere might be other mistakes too, but I don't know.",
